{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793513529,"nonce":"HSorO0Kp+rD88j8YWaVfC40oIlE=","title":"M4: VIR, extraction of the pure subset, semantics library v0, translation, differential testing","message":"Parent epic: listed in a comment below. Depends on M3. Next milestone to start.\n\n\nThe kernel can check CIC, but nothing yet turns C# into CIC. M4 builds the frontend for pure code (design §3.2, §4, §6).\n\n\n```text\npseudocode (design §4):\n    C# method  --Roslyn IOperation/CFG--\u003e  LeanSharp.Extraction\n               --\u003e VIR unit (typed, structured, canonical encoding, content hash)\n               --LeanSharp.Semantics--\u003e Lean definitions over the LeanSharp Lean library\n               --\u003e kernel admits the definitions; theorems closed by rfl/decide\n```\n\nPieces:\n\n- `LeanSharp` user API (netstandard2.0): `[Verified]`, `[Theorem]`, `Spec.*`, `Prove` (target syntax, design §5; still open).\n- `LeanSharp.Vir`: the IR and its canonical JSON/binary encoding.\n- `LeanSharp.Extraction`: the pure subset only: `int`/`long`/`bool`, records, `if`/`switch`, recursion.\n- `lean/LeanSharp/` semantics library v0 (D10): faithful models (`int` → `Int32` with wrap-around, D7), built with Lean at development time and shipped as an NDJSON bundle re-checked by our kernel.\n- `LeanSharp.Semantics`: shallow, syntax-directed translation (`if` → `ite`/`dite`, `switch` → match, recursion → structural or well-founded with `Spec.Decreases`).\n- Differential tests: compiled .NET results vs kernel evaluation of the model on generated inputs (design §10.5).\n\n\n`[Verified]` pure methods translate, and differential tests pass. Theorems are closed by `rfl`/`decide`.\n\n\n- Whether `LeanSharp.Meta` adds a metavariable kind to `LeanSharp.Cic.Expr` (kernel rejects it) or keeps its own representation (design §7.1).\n- Open questions §12 that touch the pure subset: enums open vs `[Closed]` (Q3), Lean version pin (Q10), target framework (Q13).\n\nStatus: not started.","files":null}]}